    excerpt: "Insurable is not financeable. Insurable means that a governable spend system can be underwritten so residual risk after enforceable stops is transferable to a counterparty, by an executed insurability instrument. Financeable means that an insurable residual-risk cover can be funded or underwritten for the next draw against named cash-flow evidence, covenants, and recourse, by an executed financeability instrument: a named lender or capital commitment, covenants that bind that draw to the insurable cover, recourse terms naming who pays if the cover does not respond, or an underwriting memo that funds the next draw only when that evidence is on the file. An insurance certificate with no counterparty committed to fund the next draw, a cover limit with no cash-flow evidence a lender will underwrite, a binder without covenants or recourse, or a claims pack that cannot support the next draw is not financeable.",
