    description: "Sustained is not scaled. Sustained means, on the industrial scale spine, instrument-required sustainment that holds the accepted or operated successor outcome in evidenced continuity under real operating load across the named sustain window — evidenced by sustainment package with named sustainer / owner roles, named sustainment criteria met (accepted or operated package cited, next sustain window named, operating-load continuity the outcome must hold stated, residual ownership still named), dates, and an unbroken trail from that accepted or operated evidence to that sustainment evidence — not a dashboard green tile with no sustainment authority, not a verbal \"we sustained it,\" not extending a sustain memo with no instrument path, not a chat note that says sustained, and not treating a one-site clear as automatic continuity under load. Scaled means, under that same named instrument for that channel, instrument-required scale that multiplies that sustained outcome across additional sites, crews, assets, or volume with the same evidence bar, ownership, and control integrity intact across the next named scale window — evidenced by scale package with named scale owner / site / crew / asset / volume roles, named scale criteria met (sustainment package cited, next scale window named, evidence bar the sustainment must carry intact across additional sites, crews, assets, or volume stated, ownership and control integrity still named), dates, and an unbroken trail from the sustainment evidence to that scale evidence — not a local sustain win treated as a fleet rollout, not a dashboard green multiplied by site count, not a pilot copy-paste, not a verbal \"we scaled it,\" and not a slide that copies one site's green tile into a fleet count. Sustained is not scaled. A firm can be sustained and still not scaled (sustainment evidence exists while required scale evidence for the next scale window is missing). A firm can hold evidenced continuity under real operating load across the named sustain window and still lack instrument-required scale that multiplies that sustained outcome across additional sites, crews, assets, or volume with the same evidence bar, ownership, and control integrity intact. A firm can claim scale theater and still not be sustained (a dashboard green multiplied by site count, a pilot copy-paste, or a fleet rollout of a local win while required sustainment evidence is missing). Sustainment evidence alone is not scale of that sustained successor outcome. A scale claim alone is not proof the named sustainment evidence was on the file. A local sustain that dies when copied is not scaled reliability. A CMMS checkbox, ticket state, status light, dashboard sustained tile, verbal \"we sustained it,\" dashboard green multiplied by site count, pilot copy-paste, or fleet-rollout note alone is neither. A verbal \"we scaled it\" alone is neither. Keep this sustained distinct from the successor-spine Operated Is Not Sustained and from Sustained Is Not Assured. Keep this sustained distinct from the filing-spine Sustained Is Not Scaled and from Adopted Is Not Sustained. Keep this scaled distinct from the filing-spine Scaled Is Not Compounded. This essay does not give that sustained a new meaning inside Operated Is Not Sustained or Sustained Is Not Assured. This essay does not rewrite those theses. This split is sustained versus scaled. This essay separates instrument-required sustainment that holds the accepted or operated successor outcome in evidenced continuity under real operating load across the named sustain window from instrument-required scale that multiplies that sustained outcome across additional sites, crews, assets, or volume with the same evidence bar, ownership, and control integrity intact across the next named scale window. Evidence from the plant beats the sustainment record when the record is being used as scaled. Evidence from the plant beats the scale claim when the claim is being used as proof the named sustainment of that successor outcome was on the file. Sync refuses to pretend sustained or scaled is a status light. Sync does not measure scaled. Sync does not measure scaled for the customer. Sync does not measure sustained or scaled for the customer. Sync may surface a sustainment record or a scale record beside Evidence, Verification, and the closed outcome. Sync must not treat sustained as scaled as Learning credit. Sync does not deem scaled for the customer. Sync must not auto-deem-scaled. A practice record that says sustained is scaled is not shown scaled. This sustained is evidenced continuity under real operating load on the industrial scale spine. It is not the filing-spine hold of an adopted practice in Sustained Is Not Scaled, and it is not the continued-force register hold Operated Is Not Sustained or Sustained Is Not Assured names. This essay does not collapse into Sustained Is Not Scaled. This essay does not rewrite Sustained Is Not Scaled. This essay does not collapse into Scaled Is Not Compounded. This essay does not rewrite Scaled Is Not Compounded. This essay does not claim a successor route for Scaled Is Not Compounded. This essay does not collapse into Transferable Is Not Binding. This essay does not rewrite Transferable Is Not Binding. This essay does not collapse into Binding Is Not Enforced. This essay does not rewrite Binding Is Not Enforced. This essay does not restate Transferable Is Not Binding or Binding Is Not Enforced as this claim. This essay does not collapse sustained into scaled. This essay does not collapse scaled into sustained. A local sustain that dies when copied is not scaled reliability.",
